    markdown: "### **Frequently Asked Questions**\n\n#### **Does Servana process payments inside the platform?**\n\nNo. Servana records and validates offline payments. Your clients can pay through methods such as cash, M-Pesa, bank transfer, card terminal, voucher, split payment, or another merchant-defined offline method. \n\n#### **Can Front Office record payment details?**\n\nYes, where permitted. Front Office can record payment details, but Finance is responsible for validating payment truth, especially for high-risk or merchant-configured payment states. \n\n#### **Can receipts be generated before payment is validated?**\n\nReceipts should not be generated before payment is marked as received or validated, depending on the merchant’s configuration. \n\n#### **Can Merchant Finance see commissions?**\n\nYes. Merchant Finance can view commission liabilities so the business has clearer visibility over what may be owed to personnel.\n\n#### **Is the Finance account separate from other merchant users?**\n\nYes. Servana uses role-based access so Finance users can focus on payment validation, records, receipts, reports, balances, commissions, and financial activity without needing full control over every merchant operation.\n\n#### **How does a Finance user get access?**\n\nThe Merchant Administrator creates or activates the Merchant Finance user under the merchant account. The user then logs in through Magic Link after their email and role are active.\n\n---",
